        "original_id": "990afafe-8620-5bd5-a734-2b5a21ed624b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Ella Fitzgerald, Louis Armstrong, Dave Barbour\n- Organizations: Decca\n- Roles: jazz singer\n- Works: \"Would You Like to Take a Walk?\"\n- Concepts: honorific nicknames\n\nFacts:\n- Ella Jane Fitzgerald was born on April 25, 1917, and died on June 15, 1996.\n- Ella Fitzgerald was an African-American jazz singer.\n- Ella Fitzgerald was often referred to as the First Lady of Song, the Queen of Jazz, and Lady Ella.\n- In 1951, Ella Fitzgerald and Louis Armstrong recorded \"Would You Like to Take a Walk?\" for Decca.\n- The 1951 Decca recording of \"Would You Like to Take a Walk?\" by Ella Fitzgerald and Louis Armstrong was accompanied by the Dave Barbour Orchestra.",
